<!--
  DataAgent marketing site - sitemap.xml

  ONE VALUE TO CHANGE WHEN THE SITE IS DEPLOYED
  ===============================================
  The domain below (dataagent.example) is a PLACEHOLDER. The .example TLD is
  reserved by RFC 2606, so it can never resolve to a real host.

  It is in EIGHTEEN files, not two: this file, website/robots.txt, and all
  sixteen HTML pages - each of which carries it in its og:url and og:image
  tags. The og:url is the link a visitor sees when the page is shared, so
  a deployment that misses it produces a broken preview card on every
  shared link.

  One command does all of it:

      grep -rl "dataagent\.example" website | xargs sed -i "s/dataagent\.example/YOUR-DOMAIN/g"

  The site URL is NOT derived from window.DATAAGENT_REPO_URL in
  website/js/main.js: that constant is the GitHub repository that publishes
  the Windows releases, not the web host.

  The two error pages (404.html, 403.html) are deliberately NOT listed: they
  are marked noindex and they are not content. Every other page in
  website/ is listed exactly once.
-->
